{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1413690-changeling-mage-crossover-discussion","id":1413690,"title":"Changeling Mage Crossover Discussion!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T19:51:49-07:00","id":1413690,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Changeling Mage Crossover Discussion!","content":"I made a Twin thread over at the<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413682-mage-changeling-crossover-discussion\"> Mage Forum. </a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Of all the gamelines I think Mage and Changeling would fit the most seemlessly together even in a combined group. So what would be the pros and cons of running a Changeling Mage Crossover game? What about using the previous edition Enchanted Rules and have the Mages as Kinain, so they will be able to see chimerical reality and could even pic up Arts. What are the of things that you could do when Mage Spheres/Pillars combine with Fae Arts towards the same goal? Kinain or Enchanted Mages feel like they could fit say a Kithain Motley perhaps even better then say Inanimae or Adhene. And one of the big things is they both have a vested interest in bringing magic back to the world. More numinous wonder could smooth the consensus and the local banality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mages can perform coincidental magic that make help lower the disbelief and banality in mortals, and Fae Arts can help usher in Mythic Strands which broadens what is considered coincidental in areas. Fae Arts with the right realms can even be cast to boost magical effects, and the same with Magick cast to help Cantrips. And I would imagine Unleashing would temporarily have some sort of beneficial effect on countering or synchronizing the immediate consensus, though it could also make magick go haywire if the Changeling looses control. Not to mention the synchronization between the Countless and Etherites and Void Engineers or Dreamspeaker and Nunnehi/Menehune/Inanimae!</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T16:11:43-07:00","id":1414085,"title":"","content":"(The following is something I wrote about ten years ago, mainly as a mental/creative exercise, in which I did outlines for a series of crossover books for each of the original five game lines. The four Changeling related books I ended up giving a set of thematically linked titles, Midnight Masquerade, Savage Dawn, Mystic Zenith, and Shadows in Twilight. All four followed the same basic structure, as did the other six crossover book outlines.)<br /> <br /> <b>Mystic Zenith</b><br /> A crossover sourcebook for Mage: The Ascension and Changeling: The Dreaming<br /> <br /> Obligatory opening fiction and introduction/overview. <br /> <br /> <i>Chapter One: Dreams of Magic (Crossovers)</i><br /> <br /> How, where, and why Awakened and Fey encounter each other, including interactions, conflicts, and commonalities. <br /> Myths, legends, and stereotypes both groups have about the other. <br /> The prehistoric Wyck/whatever other names they may be known by and their interactions with the Fey lords of Arcadia. <br /> Stories and encounters from the mystical times before the Ascension War and the Shattering. <br /> The Dionysian Compacts between ancient Grecian Ecstatics and the Satyrs. <br /> The lost Hermetic House of Diedne and rumors of potential survivors within Arcadia or the Dreaming; House Meritina and their study of faerie magic.<br /> The Valdaerman and the ancient jotun/Trolls. <br /> The Glastonbury Compact of Britain. <br /> The Dreamspeakers and the spirit people of the ancient Americas, Africa, Asia, and Australia.<br /> The Akashic Brotherhood, the Ministry of Works and their relations with the Hsien. <br /> The Ahl i Batin and the Jinn. <br /> Wyngarde's March across Britain at the start of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> The Invisible World of the Umbra/Spirits and The Dreaming; how the two interact, blend and/or bypass each other. <br /> Mages in the Dreaming<br /> Changelings in the Umbra/Astral Realms<br /> Realms of specific note, such as the Arcadian Gateways and Balador. <br /> Changelings in the Digital Web and the idea of a Digital Dreaming.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy and the Fey<br /> Changelings as Reality Deviants, and why they are viewed as a possible vanguard for an alien/extradimensional invasion. <br /> Theories, Directives and Tactics for dealing with Changelings.<br /> Capture by the Technocracy and being overwhelmed with Banality, including potentially becoming one of the Dauntain (especially Nihilists or Typhoids). <br /> <br /> The Nephandi and the Fomorians, and what possible ties they may have with each other.<br /> <br /> The Marauders and the dangerous impact they have on the local Dreaming, as well as the increased risk of Bedlam. <br /> <br /> Enchantment and how it works (or sometimes doesn't) on the Awakened. <br /> Changelings, Kinain, Chimera, and other Enchanted as Acolytes. <br /> Why Changelings can't Awaken or do Sphere Magic.<br /> Awakened Kinain and how that works mechanically. <br /> <br /> Bygones, how they fit into Changeling's worldview, and using them in Changeling. <br /> <br /> Glamour vs Quintessence <br /> The idea of Chantries that double as Freeholds.<br /> Nodes that tap into the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Enchanted Talismans and Mystic Treasures, discussing the ins and outs of such ideas, and a couple of samples of each.<br /> <br /> The Mechanics of Sphere Magic vs Arts &amp; Realms, including how they can be used to support and bolster each other (as well as clash or nullify).<br /> Doing crossovers without bothering to use the other game's rules (ie, Changelings with Rotes/Merits and Mages with Arts). <br /> <br /> Themes and Moods of Mage/Changeling Crossovers<br /> Scale and Scope of Mage/Changeling Crossovers<br /> <br /> NPC Stock Characters for Mage/Changeling Crossover Chronicles<br /> Knight of the Dreaming - your standard would be heroic Wilder in search of adventure<br /> Troublesome Helper - the Faerie trickster <br /> Fey Sorceress <br /> Dreamborn Lover - a Kinain or Changeling acolyte/ally <br /> Asylum Escapee - Orphan or potential Dauntain<br /> Nightmare Beast - a monster of the Dreaming<br /> Classical Artisan - the typical creative type who may be human, Enchanted, Acolyte or Awakened<br /> Scholar of the Fey<br /> Technodreamer<br /> Cautious Diplomat - trying to establish relations with the other side<br /> Rampaging Marauder<br /> Mad Prophet - a powerful Changeling well in the throws of Bedlam<br /> Man in Black<br /> Enlightened Psychologist<br /> Abomination of Rationality - probably a Dauntain, perhaps even a type we've never seen before<br /> The Boogieman - a spiritual embodiment of fear<br /> Fomorian Nephandus - one of the Fallen tied with the Fomorians<br /> Dream of the Unknown Abyss - some ... thing from the deepest depths of the Dreaming or Deep Umbra. <br /> The Sleeping Dragon<br /> <br /> <i>Chapter Two: Mystic San Fransisco </i><br /> <br /> Basically the overview of the greater San Fransisco Bay area from a Mage perspective including its local leadership, legends, Bygones, places of power, Chantries, and Cabals. Also the local Umbra, spirit courts, Technocracy presence, and other dangers. <br /> <br /> <i>Chapter Three: Dreams of Seattle</i> (I picked Seattle as the Mage signature city)<br /> <br /> An overview of Seattle and the surrounding region from a Changeling perspective, with its various nobles and Freeholds, the local Nunnehi and Inanimae, the Dreaming, and various monsters, mysteries and curiosities. <br /> <br /> <i>Chapter Four: The Mad House</i><br /> A pre-made chronicle that can be run for Mage, Changeling or both, nominally set in San Fransisco or Seattle, but can easily be moved to any other moderately sized city. The basic plot is that the PCs try to rescue someone they know from a local secret asylum (ie, a prison/reeducation center run by their foes) only to find that some of the inmate may actually belong there. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, such was the outline for an imaginary book that never existed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:43:07-07:00","id":1414117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <stron