":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:22:37-07:00","id":1414349,"title":"","content":"Honestly as a brittish person Isle of the Mighty isn't that bad about it. The Scottish section is even pretty good! (They remembered that the border isn't immediently south of Edinburgh for example. Which is something even other scottish people sometimes forget.) I couldn't say for the Ireland or Wales sections but the England and Cornwall parts where also fine. Not all of the slang, place names or dialects are correct but nothing offensive, particually compered to some <i>other</i> products in the line. Its also explisitly made with Crossover play in mind which is nice. I'm using the Scotland chapter for a game right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:47:45-07:00","id":1414354,"title":"","content":"This all sounds super cool. I liked Isle of the Mighty and I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing an updated version done by real British writers for C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T06:22:35-07:00","id":1414372,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that can be that hard, my Changlings have a Mage friend that was Conditioned, there trying to help her.","signature":"","edited